  "code": "1133",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"33\" data-end=\"71\"><strong data-start=\"33\" data-end=\"71\">Purpose and Clinical Significance:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"72\" data-end=\"511\">\n<li data-start=\"72\" data-end=\"172\">\n<p data-start=\"74\" data-end=\"172\">Measures the amount of <strong data-start=\"97\" data-end=\"125\">lactic acid in the blood</strong>, which is a byproduct of anaerobic metabolism.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"173\" data-end=\"271\">\n<p data-start=\"175\" data-end=\"271\">Primarily used to assess <strong data-start=\"200\" data-end=\"218\">tissue hypoxia</strong>, <strong data-start=\"220\" data-end=\"230\">sepsis</strong>, <strong data-start=\"232\" data-end=\"241\">shock</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"247\" data-end=\"270\">metabolic disorders</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"272\" data-end=\"438\">\n<p data-start=\"274\" data-end=\"438\">Helps differentiate between <strong data-start=\"302\" data-end=\"328\">type A lactic acidosis</strong> (due to hypoxia) and <strong data-start=\"350\" data-end=\"376\">type B lactic acidosis</strong> (without obvious hypoxia, often from liver failure or drugs).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"439\" data-end=\"511\">\n<p data-start=\"441\" data-end=\"511\">Also used to monitor response to treatment in critically ill patients.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width: 19.3032%;\"><strong>Lactate Levels</strong></th>\n<th style=\"width: 80.6968%;\"><strong>Clinical Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 19.3032%;\"><strong>Elevated (&gt;2 mmol/L)</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 80.6968%;\">Suggests tissue hypoxia, sepsis, cardiogenic or hypovolemic shock, liver dysfunction, severe anemia, seizures, or mitochondrial/metabolic disorders. Can also rise with strenuous exercise, certain medications (e.g. metformin), or toxins (e.g. cyanide).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 19.3032%;\"><strong>Normal (0.5&ndash;2.0 mmol/L)</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 80.6968%;\">Indicates adequate tissue oxygenation and normal metabolism.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"513\" data-end=\"538\">&nbsp;</p>",
